---
description: Rules for working with PocketBase in Next.js
globs: next-app/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---
[nextjs.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/nextjs.mdc)

- PocketBase utilities are in `next-app/lib/pocketbase-server.ts`
- Use `createPocketBase()` to create a new PocketBase instance
- Use `initPocketBase()` to initialize PocketBase with auth from cookies (for Server Components)
- Use `getAuthenticatedUser()` to check if user is authenticated (returns `null` if not)
- Auth state is stored in HTTP-only cookies named `pb_auth`
- Cookie settings are configured via `getCookieSettings()` helper
- Always validate PocketBase records with Zod schemas before using them
- Handle `ClientResponseError` from PocketBase with proper error messages
- Use `pb.authStore.isValid` to check authentication status
- Use `pb.authStore.record` to access authenticated user record
- Call `pb.authStore.authRefresh()` to refresh expired tokens
- Clear auth store with `pb.authStore.clear()` on logout or invalid auth
